# colorcorrect

- Label: Color Correct
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 60 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/colorcorrect.html
- Summary (EN): The Color Correct node adjusts image colours with separate Shadow, Midtone and Highlight regions. A Master set of adjustments then applies to the combined result.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Color Correct règle séparément les ombres, les médiotons et les hautes lumières, puis applique un réglage maître à l'ensemble.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the original layer", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source", "Mask: blends the new values with the original, default 1; also sets the affected RGBA channels", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha", "Treat RGBA as Premultiplied: multiplies RGB by alpha", "Shadow, Midtone, Highlight: each has a toggle and Add (offset), Mult (scale), Gamma (power curve), Contrast controls", "Master: a toggle plus the same Add, Mult, Gamma, Contrast controls, applied to the combined result"]

- Caveats: ["Shadow, Midtone and Highlight are applied first and combined, then Master is applied", "If the Master or a range toggle is off, its values are removed from the final output"]

